IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-core`
IMPORT `sg-periods`
IMPORT `sg-definitions`
IMPORT `sg-interpretation`
IMPORT `sgo-penalties`
IMPORT `sgo-offences`

-- Tests for sgo-offences.l4 (ss 401 to 406).
-- Every expected value is written from the text of the section, beside the assertion, before the code was run.
-- An unmet element of an offence answers NOTHING (the section says "shall be guilty" of the person who does the act and is silent about anyone else).

§ `Section 401(1): a misleading statement of the amount of capital`

-- Arguments of the corporation: advertises or publishes a statement of its capital; the statement is misleading; the amount of capital or subscribed capital is stated; the paid-up capital or the charge on uncalled capital is not stated as prominently.
-- a misleading statement is enough.
#ASSERT `s 401(1) the corporation is guilty of an offence` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- not misleading, but the capital is stated and the paid-up amount is less prominent.
#ASSERT `s 401(1) the corporation is guilty of an offence` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- the capital is stated and the paid-up amount is as prominent: neither limb.
#ASSERT `s 401(1) the corporation is guilty of an offence` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- the second limb needs the capital to be stated at all.
#ASSERT `s 401(1) the corporation is guilty of an offence` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- no statement of capital advertised or published.
#ASSERT `s 401(1) the corporation is guilty of an offence` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 401(1) the corporation is guilty of an offence` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- Arguments of the officer: the four facts above; then whether the officer knowingly authorises, directs or consents.
#ASSERT `s 401(1) the officer of the corporation is guilty of an offence` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 401(1) the officer of the corporation is guilty of an offence` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- not knowingly: the officer is not caught.
#ASSERT `s 401(1) the officer of the corporation is guilty of an offence` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- no statement published, so there is nothing to authorise.
#ASSERT `s 401(1) the officer of the corporation is guilty of an offence` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- a statement that is neither misleading nor less prominent.
#ASSERT `s 401(1) the officer of the corporation is guilty of an offence` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

-- The subsection states no penalty: s 407(2) gives a fine of at most $1,000 and no imprisonment.
#ASSERT `s 401(1) the highest penalty on conviction` TRUE EQUALS JUST (Penalty OF 1000, 0, FALSE, FALSE)
#ASSERT `s 401(1) the highest penalty on conviction` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 401(1) a corporation must not advertise a misleading statement of its capital` "Acme" AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Company "Acme" DOES `s 401(1) advertise, circulate or publish a misleading statement of the amount of capital` AT 4
-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 401(1) a corporation must not advertise a misleading statement of its capital` "Acme" AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 30

§ `Section 401(2), (2A) and (3): statements in a document`

-- (3): a vote in favour of the making of the statement is deemed to authorise it.
#ASSERT `s 401(3) the person is deemed to have authorised the making of the statement` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 401(3) the person is deemed to have authorised the making of the statement` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- Arguments of (2): the statement is in a required document; it is false or misleading in a material particular; the person knows it to be so; the person wilfully makes it; wilfully authorises it; votes in favour at a meeting; wilfully omits (or authorises the omission of) a matter without which the document is misleading in a material respect.
-- wilfully makes a false statement, knowing.
#ASSERT `s 401(2) the person is guilty of an offence` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- wilfully authorises it, knowing.
#ASSERT `s 401(2) the person is guilty of an offence` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- votes in favour at a meeting: deemed to have authorised it (fork F-401-2: the vote is read as satisfying "wilfully authorises").
#ASSERT `s 401(2) the person is guilty of an offence` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- the person does none of the three acts.
#ASSERT `s 401(2) the person is guilty of an offence` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- the person does not know the statement to be false or misleading: the first limb needs the knowledge.
#ASSERT `s 401(2) the person is guilty of an offence` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- the statement is not false or misleading in a material particular.
#ASSERT `s 401(2) the person is guilty of an offence` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- the second limb: wilfully omits a matter without which the document is misleading in a material respect; no knowledge of falsity is asked.
#ASSERT `s 401(2) the person is guilty of an offence` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- not a document required by or for the purposes of this Act.
#ASSERT `s 401(2) the person is guilty of an offence` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 401(2) the person is guilty of an offence` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

-- fine not exceeding $50,000 or imprisonment not exceeding 2 years or both.
#ASSERT `s 401(2) the highest penalty on conviction` TRUE EQUALS JUST (Penalty OF 50000, 24, TRUE, FALSE)
#ASSERT `s 401(2) the highest penalty on conviction` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 401(2) a person must not wilfully make or authorise a false or misleading statement in a required document` "Ann" AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Individual "Ann" DOES `s 401(2) wilfully make or authorise a false or misleading statement in a document required by or for the purposes of this Act` AT 2
-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 401(2) a person must not wilfully make or authorise a false or misleading statement in a required document` "Ann" AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 10

-- Arguments of (2A): lodges, files or submits a document to the Registrar; authorises another person to do so; knows the document to be false or misleading in a material respect.
#ASSERT `s 401(2A) the person is guilty of an offence` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 401(2A) the person is guilty of an offence` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- lodges it but does not know: the knowledge is an element.
#ASSERT `s 401(2A) the person is guilty of an offence` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- knows it to be false but neither lodges nor authorises.
#ASSERT `s 401(2A) the person is guilty of an offence` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 401(2A) the highest penalty on conviction` TRUE EQUALS JUST (Penalty OF 50000, 24, TRUE, FALSE)
#ASSERT `s 401(2A) the highest penalty on conviction` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 401(2A) a person must not lodge a document with the Registrar knowing it to be false or misleading` "Ann" AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Individual "Ann" DOES `s 401(2A) lodge a document with the Registrar knowing it to be false or misleading in a material respect` AT 1
-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 401(2A) a person must not lodge a document with the Registrar knowing it to be false or misleading` "Ann" AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 5

§ `Section 402: false statements or reports`

-- The seam the keel asks of this section.
#ASSERT `s 402(1) the reference is in section 402` TRUE EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 402(1) the reference is in section 402` FALSE EQUALS FALSE

-- (2): "officer" includes a person who at any time has been an officer.
#ASSERT `s 402(2) the person is within the word officer in subsection (1)` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 402(2) the person is within the word officer in subsection (1)` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- The words "relating to the affairs of the corporation" are construed by s 4(8): paragraph (a) lists the business, so a statement about it is within them.
#ASSERT `s 402(1) the statement or report relates to the affairs of the corporation` `s 4(8)(a) the promotion, formation, membership, control, business, trading, transactions, dealings, property, liabilities, profits, income, receipts, losses, outgoings or expenditure of the corporation` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- paragraph (b) names the beneficiaries of a trust: it applies where the corporation is a trustee that is not a trustee corporation.
#ASSERT `s 402(1) the statement or report relates to the affairs of the corporation` `s 4(8)(b) the identity of the beneficiaries under a trust of which the corporation is trustee, their rights and the payments they have received or are entitled to receive` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 402(1) the statement or report relates to the affairs of the corporation` `s 4(8)(b) the identity of the beneficiaries under a trust of which the corporation is trustee, their rights and the payments they have received or are entitled to receive` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- a matter outside the list: "including" leaves the list open, so the subsection says nothing.
#ASSERT `s 402(1) the statement or report relates to the affairs of the corporation` `s 4(8) some other matter` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- Arguments of (1): what the person is; has at any time been an officer; makes or furnishes with intent to deceive; knowingly and wilfully authorises or permits it; the statement is false or misleading; to whom; the corporation is a subsidiary; the statement relates to the affairs of the corporation.
-- a director who makes a false statement with intent to deceive to a member.
#ASSERT `s 402(1) the person is guilty of an offence` `s 4(1) "officer" a director of the corporation` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE `s 402(1)(a) a director, auditor, member, debenture holder or trustee for debenture holders of the corporation` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- the secretary who authorises and permits the furnishing of it, without making it.
#ASSERT `s 402(1) the person is guilty of an offence` `s 4(1) "officer" the secretary of the corporation` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE `s 402(1)(a) a director, auditor, member, debenture holder or trustee for debenture holders of the corporation` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- a former officer: (2) includes one.
#ASSERT `s 402(1) the person is guilty of an offence` `s 4(1) "officer" anyone else` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE `s 402(1)(a) a director, auditor, member, debenture holder or trustee for debenture holders of the corporation` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- someone who is not, and never was, an officer.
#ASSERT `s 402(1) the person is guilty of an offence` `s 4(1) "officer" anyone else` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE `s 402(1)(a) a director, auditor, member, debenture holder or trustee for debenture holders of the corporation` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (b): to an auditor of the holding company, in the case of a corporation that is a subsidiary.
#ASSERT `s 402(1) the person is guilty of an offence` `s 4(1) "officer" a director of the corporation` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE `s 402(1)(b) an auditor of the holding company of a corporation that is a subsidiary` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 402(1) the person is guilty of an offence` `s 4(1) "officer" a director of the corporation` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE `s 402(1)(b) an auditor of the holding company of a corporation that is a subsidiary` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- to someone else.
#ASSERT `s 402(1) the person is guilty of an offence` `s 4(1) "officer" a director of the corporation` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE `s 402(1) someone else` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- the statement is true.
#ASSERT `s 402(1) the person is guilty of an offence` `s 4(1) "officer" a director of the corporation` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE `s 402(1)(a) a director, auditor, member, debenture holder or trustee for debenture holders of the corporation` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- neither made it with intent to deceive nor authorised it.
#ASSERT `s 402(1) the person is guilty of an offence` `s 4(1) "officer" a director of the corporation` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE `s 402(1)(a) a director, auditor, member, debenture holder or trustee for debenture holders of the corporation` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- the statement does not relate to the affairs of the corporation.
#ASSERT `s 402(1) the person is guilty of an offence` `s 4(1) "officer" a director of the corporation` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE `s 402(1)(a) a director, auditor, member, debenture holder or trustee for debenture holders of the corporation` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- a receiver who is not also a manager is not an officer (s 4(1) "officer" (d)).
#ASSERT `s 402(1) the person is guilty of an offence` `s 4(1) "officer" a receiver who is not also a manager` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE `s 402(1)(a) a director, auditor, member, debenture holder or trustee for debenture holders of the corporation` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

-- fine not exceeding $10,000 or imprisonment not exceeding 2 years or both.
#ASSERT `s 402(1) the highest penalty on conviction` TRUE EQUALS JUST (Penalty OF 10000, 24, TRUE, FALSE)
#ASSERT `s 402(1) the highest penalty on conviction` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 402(1) an officer must not make a false or misleading statement or report to a director, auditor or member with intent to deceive` "Bob" AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Officer "Bob" DOES `s 402(1) make or furnish, with intent to deceive, a false or misleading statement or report relating to the affairs of the corporation` AT 3
-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 402(1) an officer must not make a false or misleading statement or report to a director, auditor or member with intent to deceive` "Bob" AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 12

§ `Section 403: dividends payable from profits only`

-- Arguments of (1): the dividend is payable to the share-holders of a company; it is paid out of profits.
#ASSERT `s 403(1) the dividend is barred because it is not payable out of profits` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- "except out of profits": a dividend paid out of profits is not barred by this subsection.
#ASSERT `s 403(1) the dividend is barred because it is not payable out of profits` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- not a dividend payable to the share-holders of a company.
#ASSERT `s 403(1) the dividend is barred because it is not payable out of profits` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 403(1) the dividend is barred because it is not payable out of profits` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 403(1) a company must not pay a dividend except out of profits` "Acme" AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Company "Acme" DOES `s 403(1) pay a dividend except out of profits` AT 6
-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 403(1) a company must not pay a dividend except out of profits` "Acme" AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 100

-- Arguments of (1A): the profits are applied towards a purchase of its own shares in accordance with ss 76B to 76G; subsection (1B) applies to the amount.
#ASSERT `s 403(1A) the profits are barred from being paid as dividends to the shareholders` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- "Subject to subsection (1B)": where (1B) applies, the bar does not.
#ASSERT `s 403(1A) the profits are barred from being paid as dividends to the shareholders` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 403(1A) the profits are barred from being paid as dividends to the shareholders` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 403(1A) the profits are barred from being paid as dividends to the shareholders` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 403(1B) subsection (1A) does not apply to the amount` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 403(1B) subsection (1A) does not apply to the amount` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 403(1C) the gains are barred from being paid as dividends to the shareholders` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 403(1C) the gains are barred from being paid as dividends to the shareholders` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- Arguments of (2): occupies the position of director; the directors are accustomed to act on the person's directions; they follow the person only because of professional advice; the person is an alternate or substitute director; the person is in direct employment of or acts for the company; is principally responsible for its management; wilfully pays or permits the dividend; the dividend is in contravention of s 403.
-- a director by position.
#ASSERT `s 403(2) the person is a director or chief executive officer who wilfully pays or permits to be paid a dividend in contravention of section 403` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- a chief executive officer who is not a director.
#ASSERT `s 403(2) the person is a director or chief executive officer who wilfully pays or permits to be paid a dividend in contravention of section 403` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- a person in accordance with whose directions the directors are accustomed to act: s 4(1) "director".
#ASSERT `s 403(2) the person is a director or chief executive officer who wilfully pays or permits to be paid a dividend in contravention of section 403` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- the directors follow the person only because the person gives professional advice: s 4(2) says the person is not regarded as one.
#ASSERT `s 403(2) the person is a director or chief executive officer who wilfully pays or permits to be paid a dividend in contravention of section 403` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- an alternate director.
#ASSERT `s 403(2) the person is a director or chief executive officer who wilfully pays or permits to be paid a dividend in contravention of section 403` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- neither a director nor a chief executive officer.
#ASSERT `s 403(2) the person is a director or chief executive officer who wilfully pays or permits to be paid a dividend in contravention of section 403` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- employed but not principally responsible for the management: not a chief executive officer.
#ASSERT `s 403(2) the person is a director or chief executive officer who wilfully pays or permits to be paid a dividend in contravention of section 403` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- a director who did not wilfully pay or permit the dividend.
#ASSERT `s 403(2) the person is a director or chief executive officer who wilfully pays or permits to be paid a dividend in contravention of section 403` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- a dividend that is not in contravention of the section.
#ASSERT `s 403(2) the person is a director or chief executive officer who wilfully pays or permits to be paid a dividend in contravention of section 403` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

#ASSERT `s 403(2)(a) the person is guilty of an offence` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 403(2)(a) the person is guilty of an offence` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- fine not exceeding $5,000 or imprisonment not exceeding 12 months: "or", not "or to both".
#ASSERT `s 403(2)(a) the highest penalty on conviction` TRUE EQUALS JUST (Penalty OF 5000, 12, FALSE, FALSE)
#ASSERT `s 403(2)(a) the highest penalty on conviction` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- (b): liable to the creditors for the debts due, to the extent the dividends paid exceeded the profits.
-- Arguments: the person is within (2); the debts due to the creditors; the dividends paid; the profits of the company.
-- the excess is 8,000 - 3,000 = 5,000; the debts due are 10,000: the liability stops at the excess.
#ASSERT `s 403(2)(b) the amount the person is liable to the creditors for` TRUE 10000 8000 3000 EQUALS JUST 5000
-- the debts due are 2,000, less than the excess of 5,000: the liability stops at the debts.
#ASSERT `s 403(2)(b) the amount the person is liable to the creditors for` TRUE 2000 8000 3000 EQUALS JUST 2000
-- the dividends paid did not exceed the profits: nothing is owed.
#ASSERT `s 403(2)(b) the amount the person is liable to the creditors for` TRUE 10000 3000 8000 EQUALS JUST 0
#ASSERT `s 403(2)(b) the amount the person is liable to the creditors for` TRUE 10000 8000 8000 EQUALS JUST 0
-- not a director or chief executive officer within (2).
#ASSERT `s 403(2)(b) the amount the person is liable to the creditors for` FALSE 10000 8000 3000 EQUALS NOTHING

-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 403(2) a director or chief executive officer must not wilfully pay or permit a dividend in contravention of section 403` "Dee" AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Director "Dee" DOES `s 403(2) wilfully pay or permit to be paid a dividend in contravention of section 403` AT 9
-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 403(2) a director or chief executive officer must not wilfully pay or permit a dividend in contravention of section 403` "Dee" AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 40

-- (3): contribution. Arguments: the whole amount is recovered from one director or chief executive officer; the other person is liable and directed or consented to the payment.
#ASSERT `s 403(3) the director or chief executive officer may recover contribution against the other person` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 403(3) the director or chief executive officer may recover contribution against the other person` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 403(3) the director or chief executive officer may recover contribution against the other person` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

-- (4): no liability extends or passes on death.
#ASSERT `s 403(4) the liability extends or passes to the person's executors or administrators or is a liability of the person's estate` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 403(4) the liability extends or passes to the person's executors or administrators or is a liability of the person's estate` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- (5): "dividend" includes bonus and payment by way of bonus.
#ASSERT `s 403(5) the payment is within the word dividend` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 403(5) the payment is within the word dividend` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 404: obtaining payment by false promise`

-- Arguments of (3): an officer or agent of a corporation; deceitful means or a false promise; intent to defraud; causes or procures money or a chattel or marketable security to be paid or delivered for the corporation.
#ASSERT `s 404(3) the person is guilty of an offence` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 404(3) the person is guilty of an offence` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 404(3) the person is guilty of an offence` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 404(3) the person is guilty of an offence` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 404(3) the person is guilty of an offence` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- fine not exceeding $15,000 or imprisonment not exceeding 5 years or both.
#ASSERT `s 404(3) the highest penalty on conviction` TRUE EQUALS JUST (Penalty OF 15000, 60, TRUE, FALSE)
#ASSERT `s 404(3) the highest penalty on conviction` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 404(3) an officer or agent must not cause money to be paid to a corporation by deceitful means or false promise` "Ann" AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Individual "Ann" DOES `s 404(3) by deceitful means or false promise and with intent to defraud, cause money to be paid or a chattel or marketable security to be delivered` AT 5
-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 404(3) an officer or agent must not cause money to be paid to a corporation by deceitful means or false promise` "Ann" AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 20

-- Arguments of (4): the trial is of a charge under s 404; a registered accountant; registered under the Accountants Act 2004 as a public accountant; the opinion is on the financial position of a company over a period the accountant audited or examined according to recognised audit practice.
#ASSERT `s 404(4) the accountant's opinion is admissible as evidence of the financial position of the company` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 404(4) the accountant's opinion is admissible as evidence of the financial position of the company` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- neither a registered nor a public accountant.
#ASSERT `s 404(4) the accountant's opinion is admissible as evidence of the financial position of the company` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- not the trial of a charge under this section.
#ASSERT `s 404(4) the accountant's opinion is admissible as evidence of the financial position of the company` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- an opinion on something the accountant did not audit or examine.
#ASSERT `s 404(4) the accountant's opinion is admissible as evidence of the financial position of the company` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 405: carrying on business without registering, and improper use of words`

-- Arguments of (1): the person is a foreign company; uses a name whose final word is Limited or Berhad (or an abbreviation, imitation or translation); holds out that the business is incorporated under the Act; at that time the business was duly incorporated under the Act.
-- paragraph (a): not a foreign company, uses such a name.
#ASSERT `s 405(1) the person is guilty of an offence` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- a foreign company is excepted from paragraph (a).
#ASSERT `s 405(1) the person is guilty of an offence` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- paragraph (b) names no exception for a foreign company.
#ASSERT `s 405(1) the person is guilty of an offence` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 405(1) the person is guilty of an offence` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- neither paragraph.
#ASSERT `s 405(1) the person is guilty of an offence` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- "unless at that time the business was duly incorporated under this Act": the person is not guilty.
#ASSERT `s 405(1) the person is guilty of an offence` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 405(1) the person is guilty of an offence` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- the "unless" only qualifies a person caught by (a) or (b).
#ASSERT `s 405(1) the person is guilty of an offence` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- fine not exceeding $10,000 or imprisonment not exceeding 2 years or both.
#ASSERT `s 405(1) the highest penalty on conviction` TRUE EQUALS JUST (Penalty OF 10000, 24, TRUE, FALSE)
#ASSERT `s 405(1) the highest penalty on conviction` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 405(1) a person must not use a name ending in Limited or Berhad, or hold out incorporation, unless the business is incorporated` "Ann" AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Individual "Ann" DOES `s 405(1) use a name ending in the word Limited or Berhad, or hold out that the business is incorporated under this Act, when it is not` AT 2
-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 405(1) a person must not use a name ending in Limited or Berhad, or hold out incorporation, unless the business is incorporated` "Ann" AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 8

-- Arguments of (2): the company uses the word "Private" or "Sendirian" in its name; it fulfils the requirements for private companies.
#ASSERT `s 405(2) the company is barred from using the word Private or Sendirian as part of its name` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- "if it does not fulfil the requirements": a company that fulfils them is not barred.
#ASSERT `s 405(2) the company is barred from using the word Private or Sendirian as part of its name` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 405(2) the company is barred from using the word Private or Sendirian as part of its name` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 405(2) the company is barred from using the word Private or Sendirian as part of its name` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 405(2) the corporation is guilty of an offence` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 405(2) the corporation is guilty of an offence` TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 405(2) the corporation is guilty of an offence` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Arguments of the officer: the two facts above; the officer knowingly and wilfully is guilty of the offence; the officer knowingly and wilfully authorises or permits it.
#ASSERT `s 405(2) the officer of the corporation is guilty of an offence` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 405(2) the officer of the corporation is guilty of an offence` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- an officer not in default (s 408(3)).
#ASSERT `s 405(2) the officer of the corporation is guilty of an offence` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 405(2) the officer of the corporation is guilty of an offence` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 405(2) the officer of the corporation is guilty of an offence` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- a fine not exceeding $5,000 and also a default penalty.
#ASSERT `s 405(2) the highest penalty on conviction` TRUE EQUALS JUST (Penalty OF 5000, 0, FALSE, TRUE)
#ASSERT `s 405(2) the highest penalty on conviction` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 405(2) a company must not use the word Private or Sendirian in its name unless it is a private company` "Acme" AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Company "Acme" DOES `s 405(2) use the word Private or Sendirian in the name of a company that does not fulfil the requirements for private companies` AT 1
-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 405(2) a company must not use the word Private or Sendirian in its name unless it is a private company` "Acme" AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 3

-- Arguments of (3): carries on a business, is the agent of one or acts on its behalf; holds out that the business is registered as a foreign company; at the material time it was not so registered.
#ASSERT `s 405(3) the person is guilty of an offence` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 405(3) the person is guilty of an offence` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 405(3) the person is guilty of an offence` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
